From 407be14cdcb9172b1d3c655898ac01eed4cb3feb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:52:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fonts: lazy-load FontFaceSet faces on match; implement
 fonts.load() and fonts.check()

FontFaces added to document.fonts without an explicit load() never took part
in font matching, so pages that register web fonts this way (Excalidraw's
Excalifont, Chrome-style lazy font registration) rendered in the fallback
font. Unloaded faces in the document's FontFaceSet are now registered with the
FontContext. Font matching treats them like the family's loaded templates
(best descriptor distance wins, unicode-range filters per codepoint) and
records the ones it selects; after each reflow script calls load() on those
faces, so they go loading -> loaded and the document re-lays out, as Chrome
does. Faces leave the registry when they start loading or are removed from
the set, and re-register when a descriptor setter changes them.

FontFaceSet.load() now implements "find the matching font faces": it parses
the font shorthand (CSS-wide keywords and var() are syntax errors, bolder and
lighter resolve against normal), matches faces of each named family by the
CSS font matching distance, filters by unicode-range against the text, loads
the matches and resolves with their [[FontStatusPromise]]s. FontFaceSet.check()
is exposed and returns false while a matching face is not loaded. @font-face
rules have no FontFace objects in this engine, so both consult the font
context for families whose stylesheet fonts are still downloading: load()
waits for the set's ready promise and check() returns false.

A FontFace whose descriptors fail to parse (new FontFace(name, "") as used
for local-font placeholders) rejected its [[FontStatusPromise]] eagerly, which
logged an unhandled rejection nobody could handle. The rejection now happens
when script first takes the promise through loaded or load(), matching when
Chrome reports it.

https://drafts.csswg.org/css-font-loading/#find-the-matching-font-faces
https://drafts.csswg.org/css-font-loading/#dom-fontfaceset-check

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
